---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="About nth degree and the person behind it">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="content">
    <p>
      nth degree is a personal blog about infrastructure, networking, homelab engineering,
      and systems thinking. Expect specifics over generalities — real configs, real problems,
      real solutions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every setup here runs in a Proxmox cluster in my garage. The writing covers what I've
      actually built, broken, and fixed: bare-metal networking, container orchestration,
      monitoring stacks, storage, and the thousand small decisions that make a lab hum.
    </p>

    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Static site</strong> — Astro / TypeScript, deployed via Cloudflare Workers</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting</strong> — Cloudflare edge network</li>
      <li><strong>Source</strong> — GitHub, with pre-commit checks for quality and AI-tell detection</li>
      <li><strong>No CSS frameworks, no JS in the browser</strong> — minimal footprint by design</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Writing philosophy</h2>
    <p>
      Single ideas per post. No intro that restates the title. No bullet-point takeaways.
      Prefer specifics: <q>Caddy with a Let's Encrypt TLS cert</q> over <q>good security.</q>
      If you want fluff, this isn't the place.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Typeset in <a href="https://rsms.me/inter/">Inter</a> with
      <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/">JetBrains Mono</a> for code.
      Colors adapt to your system light/dark preference.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
